{"type":"exercise","type_name":"Exercise","number":"","title":"A2","title_html":"A2","html":"<p>A quartic is fitted in the raw powers and again in the orthonormal\npolynomials of the design. Which of these differ between the two fits:\nthe linear coefficient, the fitted value at <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"x_1\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msub><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-script></mjx-msub></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>, the residual sum of squares, the\nsequential sum of squares for degree 3, the leverage <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"h_{11}\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msub><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c210E TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em;\"><mjx-TeXAtom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-TeXAtom></mjx-script></mjx-msub></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>11</mn></mrow></msub></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>, the condition number of <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"\\mathbf{X}\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-TeXAtom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D417 TEX-B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-TeXAtom></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">X</mi></mrow></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>?</p>","file":"ch42-polynomials-piecewise/02-orthogonal-polynomials.html"}